DAY 35 - PART B: LAB (CHECKPOINT PROJECT)
A secure, governed team namespace
Time: 120 minutes
==================================================================

Use the Calico cluster (NetworkPolicies must be enforced):
  kubectx kind-calico

mkdir -p ~/k8s-journey/manifests/week5/team && cd $_

Write every file yourself. Use earlier days only if stuck.


STEP 1: Namespace with Pod Security
-----------------------------------
namespace.yaml: Namespace "team-blue" with labels
  pod-security.kubernetes.io/enforce: restricted
  team: blue


STEP 2: Guardrails
------------------
quota.yaml (ResourceQuota): pods 10, requests.cpu 2, requests.memory 2Gi,
  limits.memory 4Gi, services 5
limits.yaml (LimitRange): default requests 100m/128Mi, default limits
  500m/256Mi, max memory 1Gi


STEP 3: Identities
------------------
rbac.yaml:
  - ServiceAccount "ci-deployer" + RoleBinding to ClusterRole "edit"
  - RoleBinding of ClusterRole "view" to User "auditor"
  - ServiceAccount "web" for the app (automountServiceAccountToken: false)


STEP 4: Network
---------------
netpol.yaml:
  - default deny Ingress + Egress
  - allow DNS egress to kube-dns
  - allow ingress to app=web on port 8080 from pods labelled app=client
    in the same namespace


STEP 5: The hardened app
------------------------
app.yaml: Deployment "web", 2 replicas, image
  nginxinc/nginx-unprivileged:1.27 (listens on 8080 as non-root),
  serviceAccountName web, label app=web, with:
  - requests and memory limit
  - readiness + liveness httpGet / on 8080
  - securityContext that satisfies "restricted"
  - readOnlyRootFilesystem with emptyDir mounted at /tmp
    (nginx-unprivileged writes its cache/pid under /tmp)
  - topologySpreadConstraints across hostnames
plus a Service "web" port 80 -> 8080.


STEP 6: Apply and prove each control
------------------------------------
k apply -f namespace.yaml && k apply -f .
k get all -n team-blue

Write the command and result for each test:

Quota/limits:
  [ ] k describe quota -n team-blue shows usage
  [ ] a pod asking for 2Gi memory limit is rejected (LimitRange max)

RBAC:
  [ ] k auth can-i create deploy -n team-blue --as=system:serviceaccount:team-blue:ci-deployer   -> yes
  [ ] k auth can-i delete pods -n team-blue --as=auditor   -> no
  [ ] k auth can-i get pods -n team-blue --as=auditor      -> yes
  [ ] k auth can-i get secrets -n team-blue --as=auditor   -> no

Pod Security:
  [ ] k run bad -n team-blue --image=nginx:1.27 -> rejected

Network (client pod must also satisfy "restricted"!):
  k run client -n team-blue --image=busybox:1.36 --labels=app=client \
    --overrides='{"spec":{"securityContext":{"runAsNonRoot":true,"runAsUser":1000,"seccompProfile":{"type":"RuntimeDefault"}},"containers":[{"name":"client","image":"busybox:1.36","command":["sleep","3600"],"securityContext":{"allowPrivilegeEscalation":false,"capabilities":{"drop":["ALL"]}}}]}}'
  k run other -n team-blue ... (same, but --labels=app=other)

  You need an EGRESS rule too: allow app=client egress to app=web:8080
  (add it to netpol.yaml).

  [ ] k exec -n team-blue client -- wget -qO- -T 2 web     -> OK
  [ ] k exec -n team-blue other  -- wget -qO- -T 2 web     -> blocked

Health:
  [ ] both web pods READY 1/1, spread over 2 nodes


